title: Script_2_2
---
<<enum TypeOfCocktail>>
    <<case None>>
    <<case HighAlcohol>>
    <<case LowAlcohol>>
    <<case NoneAlcohol>>
    <<case NotMatch>>
<<endenum>>
<<enum Satisfaction>>
    <<case None>>
    <<case Fail>>
    <<case Acceptable>>
    <<case Perfect>>
<<endenum>>
<<enum NPC_Name>>
    <<case None>>
    <<case Cole>>
    <<case Owen>>
    <<case Walter>>
    <<case Freya>>
    <<case Isla>>
<<endenum>>
<<enum LookDirection>>
    <<case None>>
    <<case Right>>
    <<case Left>>
    <<case Forward>>
<<endenum>>
// Declare the variable (set false by default)
<<declare $task_done = false>>
<<declare $type_of_cocktail = TypeOfCocktail.None>>
<<declare $satisfaction = Satisfaction.None>>

<<Enable_InteractableObject SystemGame false>>
<<Fix_Camera CamController true>>
<<Reset_Camera CamController>>
<<Switch_Camera CamController "MainCam">>

<<jump ShowcaseMain>>


===

title: TestLoopPart
---
// <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Owen "happy">>
// <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Cole "upset">>
// <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Owen "neutral">>

// Test part Cole {Order_Cocktail_OutName(NPC_Name.Cole)}
// Test part Owen {Order_Cocktail_OutName(NPC_Name.Owen)}
// Test part Walter {Order_Cocktail_OutName(NPC_Name.Walter)}
// Test part Freya {Order_Cocktail_OutName(NPC_Name.Freya)}
// Test part Isla {Order_Cocktail_OutName(NPC_Name.Isla)}

// Test part Cole {Order_Cocktail_OutDescription(NPC_Name.Cole)}
// Test part Owen {Order_Cocktail_OutDescription(NPC_Name.Owen)}
// Test part Walter {Order_Cocktail_OutDescription(NPC_Name.Walter)}
// Test part Freya {Order_Cocktail_OutDescription(NPC_Name.Freya)}
// Test part Isla {Order_Cocktail_OutDescription(NPC_Name.Isla)}

// ── Owen Arrives ──────────────────────────────────────────
<<Fix_Camera CamController true>>
<<Reset_Camera CamController>>
<<Switch_Camera CamController "MainCam">>

<<MoveIn NPC_Name.Owen 2>>
<<Switch_Camera CamController "CenterCam">>
<<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Owen "happy">>
<<SetLookDirection NPC_Name.Owen LookDirection.Right>>
<<wait 0.6>>
<<SetLookDirection NPC_Name.Owen LookDirection.Left>>
<<wait 0.6>>
<<SetLookDirection NPC_Name.Owen LookDirection.Forward>>
Owen: Hey! You must be the new bartender everyone's been talking about.
Owen: Place looks good. Someone's been busy.

-> Thanks, still getting used to it.
    Player: Thanks, still finding my feet honestly.
    <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Owen "happy">>
    Owen: Ha! You'll be fine. First week's always the hardest.
-> I've been here a while actually.
    Player: I've been here longer than you'd think.
    Owen: Oh! My bad, you just look fresh. Good thing I didn't say anything rude then, eh?
-> Option 3
    Player: I've been here longer than you'd think.
    Owen: Oh! My bad, you just look fresh. Good thing I didn't say anything rude then, eh?
-> Option 4
    Player: I've been here longer than you'd think.
    Owen: Oh! My bad, you just look fresh. Good thing I didn't say anything rude then, eh?

// ── Owen's Order ──────────────────────────────────────────
Owen: Anyway — could you make me something? I'm thinking {Order_Cocktail_OutName(NPC_Name.Owen)}.

<<Reset_Camera CamController>>
<<Switch_Camera CamController "MainCam">>
<<Fix_Camera CamController false>>
<<wait_for_task SystemGame>>
<<Fix_Camera CamController true>>
<<Switch_Camera CamController "CenterCam">>

<<if $satisfaction == Satisfaction.Perfect>>
    <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Owen "happy">>
    Owen: Wow. NOW that is a drink. You're good at this.
    Owen: Seriously, where did you learn that?
    -> Just picked it up.
        Player: Honestly just picked it up as I went.
        Owen: Natural talent. Love to see it.
    -> Had a good teacher.
        Player: I had someone show me the ropes early on.
        Owen: Smart. Always learn from the best.
<<elseif $satisfaction == Satisfaction.Acceptable>>
    <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Owen "neutral">>
    Owen: Hmm... not bad. I've had better, but I've had worse.
    Owen: Maybe a little less of the mixer next time?
    -> I'll keep that in mind.
        Player: Noted, I'll adjust next time.
        Owen: That's the spirit. Don't let it get to you.
    -> You're a tough crowd.
        Player: Wow, tough crowd.
        <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Owen "happy">>
        Owen: Ha! You have no idea, mate.
<<elseif $satisfaction == Satisfaction.Fail>>
    <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Owen "upset">>
    Owen: Ugh... that's rough, mate. Really rough.
    Owen: What did you even put in there?
    -> I might have overdone it.
        Player: Yeah... I think I overdid something.
        <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Owen "neutral">>
        Owen: A little, yeah. Try again sometime — I don't give up easy.
    -> Sorry, still learning.
        Player: Sorry, still learning the recipes.
        <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Owen "neutral">>
        Owen: It's fine. Just maybe don't serve that one to Walter.
<<endif>>

<<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Owen "neutral">>
<<Reset_Variable SystemGame>>

// ── Walter Arrives ────────────────────────────────────────
Owen: Oh, looks like someone's coming in.

-> Who is it?
    Owen: See for yourself...
-> A new customer?
    Owen: Nah, it's just Walter. The old man himself.

<<MoveIn NPC_Name.Walter 1>>
<<SetLookDirection NPC_Name.Walter LookDirection.Right>>
<<Switch_Camera CamController "NearLeftCam">>
<<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Walter "happy">>
Walter: Well, well — Owen! Didn't expect to see you here on a weekday.
<<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Owen "happy">>
Owen: Walter! You look terrible, old man.
Walter: Ha! And you look like you haven't changed since high school.
Owen: I'll take that as a compliment.
Walter: It wasn't one.

<<SetLookDirection NPC_Name.Walter LookDirection.Forward>>
Walter: And you must be the new bartender. Good to meet you, kid.

-> Nice to meet you too.
    Player: Nice to meet you, sir.
    <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Walter "happy">>
    Walter: "Sir"! Oh I like this one, Owen. Very respectful.
    <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Owen "happy">>
    Owen: Don't let it go to your head, Walter.
-> I've heard a lot about you.
    Player: I've actually heard a lot about you.
    Walter: Oh? Good things I hope.
    <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Owen "happy">>
    Owen: Absolutely not.
    <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Walter "happy">>
    Walter: Ha! Sounds about right.

// ── Walter's Order ────────────────────────────────────────
Walter: Right then — I'll have something, and make it better than whatever you gave Owen. Ha!
<<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Owen "neutral">>
Owen: Hey, mine was fine.
Walter: Sure it was, son.
Walter: I'm after {Order_Cocktail_OutDescription(NPC_Name.Walter)}.

<<Reset_Camera CamController>>
<<Switch_Camera CamController "MainCam">>
<<Fix_Camera CamController false>>
<<wait_for_task SystemGame>>
<<Fix_Camera CamController true>>
<<Switch_Camera CamController "NearLeftCam">>

<<if $satisfaction == Satisfaction.Perfect>>
    <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Walter "happy">>
    Walter: Now THAT takes me back. Just like the old days. Well done, kid.
    Owen: Okay... I'll admit that looks better than mine.
    Walter: It IS better than yours, Owen.
    <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Owen "upset">>
    Owen: I didn't ask, Walter.
    <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Walter "happy">>
    Walter: Ha! That's the spirit. Don't let an old man get to you.
    <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Owen "neutral">>
    Owen: You're insufferable, you know that?
    Walter: And yet here you are, still talking to me.
<<elseif $satisfaction == Satisfaction.Acceptable>>
    <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Walter "neutral">>
    Walter: Decent enough. A little more practice and you'll get there.
    Owen: See? He's tough to please.
    Walter: I'm not tough, I just have standards.
    <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Owen "happy">>
    Owen: Same thing, old man.
    Walter: You'd know nothing about standards, Owen.
    Owen: ...Rude.
<<elseif $satisfaction == Satisfaction.Fail>>
    <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Walter "upset">>
    Walter: Oh dear... that's not quite it, is it.
    <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Owen "happy">>
    Owen: Ha! So mine wasn't that bad after all.
    <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Walter "neutral">>
    Walter: Don't get smug, Owen. Yours wasn't great either.
    Owen: I'll take a partial win.
    Walter: Keep at it, kid. You'll get there.
<<endif>>

// ── Wrap Up ───────────────────────────────────────────────
<<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Walter "neutral">>
<<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Owen "neutral">>
<<Reset_Variable SystemGame>>

Walter: You know, I used to come to this place years ago. Before your time.
Owen: What was it like back then?
Walter: Quieter. Simpler. Different bartender obviously.
Owen: Better or worse?
Walter: ...Different.

-> Will you come back?
    Player: Will you be coming back?
    <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Walter "happy">>
    Walter: If the drinks keep improving? Absolutely.
    Owen: I'll be back tomorrow. Assuming Walter doesn't scare you off.
    Walter: When have I ever scared anyone off?
    <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Owen "happy">>
    Owen: Should I get the list?
-> Glad you both stopped by.
    Player: Well, glad you both came in today.
    <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Walter "happy">>
    Walter: Likewise, kid. You've got potential.
    <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Owen "happy">>
    Owen: Don't let him fool you — that's basically a standing ovation from Walter.
    Walter: ...Don't push it, Owen.

<<Switch_Camera CamController "MainCam">>
<<MoveOut NPC_Name.Walter>>
<<MoveOut NPC_Name.Owen>>

NOW IT WILL LOOP
<<jump TestLoopPart>>
===

title: ShowcaseMain
---
// ── [Setup Camera] ────────────────────────────────────────
<<Enable_InteractableObject SystemGame false>>
<<Fix_Camera CamController true>>
<<Reset_Camera CamController>>
<<Switch_Camera CamController "MainCam">>

// ── [SHOWCASE: MoveIn + SetEmotion + Switch_Camera] ──────
// Owen arrives at position 2 → CenterCam
<<MoveIn NPC_Name.Owen 2>>
<<Switch_Camera CamController "CenterCam">>
<<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Owen "happy">>
// Owen: Evening! Slow night?

// // ── [SHOWCASE: Basic Option — 4 ตัวเลือก] ───────────────
// -> Pretty quiet yeah.
//     Player: Yeah, been pretty slow tonight.
//     Owen: Good. Means I get the good seat.
// -> Just picking up actually.
//     Player: Actually just starting to get busy.
//     <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Owen "neutral">>
//     Owen: Of course it is. I have that effect on places.
// -> Depends who's asking.
//     Player: Depends who's asking.
//     <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Owen "happy">>
//     Owen: Ha! Mysterious. I like it.
// -> Not saying.
//     Player: ...
//     Owen: Fair enough.

// ── [SHOWCASE: MoveIn NPC ที่ 2 + NearLeftCam] ───────────
// Isla arrives at position 1
<<MoveIn NPC_Name.Isla 1>>
<<Switch_Camera CamController "NearLeftCam">>
<<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Isla "happy">>
<<SetLookDirection NPC_Name.Isla LookDirection.Right>>
// Isla: Oh! Owen! Didn't know you'd be here tonight.
// <<SetLookDirection NPC_Name.Owen LookDirection.Left>>
// Owen: Isla! Small world.
// Isla: Or small bar.

// Isla: Bartender — can I get something? I'm not sure what I want though...
// <<SetLookDirection NPC_Name.Isla LookDirection.Forward>>
// // ── [SHOWCASE: Option Timeout — ? และ #fallback] ─────────
// -> Any recommendations tonight? ?
//     Player: We've got some great specials on.
//     <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Isla "happy">>
//     Isla: Ooh, surprise me then!
// -> Something light maybe? ?
//     Player: I'd suggest something light and refreshing.
//     Isla: That sounds perfect actually.
// -> Something strong? ?
//     Player: Or I could go stronger if you'd like.
//     <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Isla "neutral">>
//     Isla: Hmm... maybe not tonight.
// -> Whatever you think suits me. #fallback
//     Player: I'll pick what suits you best.
//     Isla: Love the confidence!

// ── [SHOWCASE: Order_Cocktail_OutName + wait_for_task] ───
<<SetLookDirection NPC_Name.Owen LookDirection.Forward>>
Owen: This is [b]my line[/b] with [b][i]some[/i] markup within[/b] of it.
Owen: this is [s]stringk[/s] 
Owen: Right, since we're here — I'll have  [oreder]{Order_Cocktail_OutName(NPC_Name.Owen)}[/oreder], please.

<<Reset_Camera CamController>>
<<Switch_Camera CamController "MainCam">>
<<Fix_Camera CamController false>>
<<wait_for_task SystemGame>>
<<Fix_Camera CamController true>>
<<Switch_Camera CamController "CenterCam">>

// ── [SHOWCASE: Satisfaction If/Else — Owen] ───────────────
<<if $satisfaction == Satisfaction.Perfect>>
    <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Owen "happy">>
    Owen: Now THAT is exactly what I wanted. Spot on.
    <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Isla "happy">>
    Isla: Ooh, that looks good. Mine better be just as good.
    Owen: No pressure.
    -> I've been practising.
        Player: Been working on that one.
        Owen: It shows. Seriously.
    -> Lucky guess.
        Player: Honestly? Lucky guess.
        <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Owen "happy">>
        Owen: Ha! I'll take it either way.
<<elseif $satisfaction == Satisfaction.Acceptable>>
    <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Owen "neutral">>
    Owen: Not bad. Could be a touch stronger but I won't complain.
    <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Isla "neutral">>
    Isla: He's being generous, trust me.
    Owen: I heard that, Isla.
    -> I'll dial it up next time.
        Player: Noted — stronger next round.
        Owen: That's what I like to hear.
    -> This is how it's meant to be.
        Player: Actually that's the correct recipe.
        <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Owen "happy">>
        Owen: ...Fair point. I'll allow it.
<<elseif $satisfaction == Satisfaction.Fail>>
    <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Owen "upset">>
    Owen: Oh. Oh no. What... what is this?
    <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Isla "neutral">>
    Isla: Should I be worried about my order?
    Owen: Very.
    -> Sorry, let me redo it.
        Player: That one's on me. Let me fix it.
        <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Owen "neutral">>
        Owen: Please. Quickly.
    -> It's an acquired taste.
        Player: It's a bold flavour profile.
        <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Owen "upset">>
        Owen: It's a crime against cocktails is what it is.
<<endif>>

<<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Owen "neutral">>
<<Reset_Variable SystemGame>>

// ── [SHOWCASE: Order_Cocktail_OutDescription] ────────────
Isla: Okay my turn! Something {Order_Cocktail_OutDescription(NPC_Name.Isla)}, please!
<<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Isla "happy">>

<<Reset_Camera CamController>>
<<Switch_Camera CamController "MainCam">>
<<Fix_Camera CamController false>>
<<wait_for_task SystemGame>>
<<Fix_Camera CamController true>>
<<Switch_Camera CamController "NearLeftCam">>

// ── [SHOWCASE: Satisfaction If/Else — Isla] ───────────────
<<if $satisfaction == Satisfaction.Perfect>>
    <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Isla "happy">>
    Isla: This is AMAZING. Owen, try this!
    <<SetLookDirection NPC_Name.Isla LookDirection.Right>>
    <<SetLookDirection NPC_Name.Owen LookDirection.Left>>
    Owen: ...Okay fine. *sip* ...Yeah. That's actually good.
    Isla: Right?!
    -> Really glad that hit the mark.
        Player: Really glad that hit the mark.
        Isla: Hit the mark? It hit a bullseye!
    -> Owen's reaction says it all.
        Player: Owen's face said everything I needed to know.
        <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Owen "neutral">>
        Owen: I said nothing.
        <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Isla "happy">>
        Isla: Your eyes said everything, Owen.
<<elseif $satisfaction == Satisfaction.Acceptable>>
    <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Isla "neutral">>
    Isla: Mmm... it's nice! Just a little sweet for me.
    <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Owen "happy">>
    Owen: She hates sweet things by the way.
    <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Isla "neutral">>
    Isla: Owen!
    Owen: What? It's true!
    -> I'll remember that — less sweet next time.
        Player: Noted. Less sweet next round.
        <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Isla "happy">>
        Isla: You're very thoughtful, thank you.
    -> Round two on me.
        Player: Let me make it up to you.
        Isla: Now we're talking.
<<elseif $satisfaction == Satisfaction.Fail>>
    <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Isla "upset">>
    Isla: Um... this is... interesting.
    <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Owen "happy">>
    Owen: Ha! Welcome to my world, Isla.
    <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Isla "neutral">>
    Isla: Is it always like this?
    Owen: First round jitters. Probably.
    -> I'm really sorry about that.
        Player: I'm really sorry about that one.
        <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Isla "happy">>
        Isla: It's okay! Everyone has off days.
    -> The next one will be better.
        Player: Trust me, the next one will be better.
        Isla: It can only go up from here, right?
        <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Owen "happy">>
        Owen: Statistically yes.
<<endif>>

<<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Isla "neutral">>
<<Reset_Variable SystemGame>>

// ── [SHOWCASE: MoveIn NPC ที่ 3 + SetLookDirection] ──────
// Walter arrives at position 3
Isla: Oh — someone just walked in.

<<MoveIn NPC_Name.Walter 3>>
<<Switch_Camera CamController "CenterCam">>
<<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Walter "neutral">>
Walter: Evening all. Don't mind me.

<<SetLookDirection NPC_Name.Owen LookDirection.Right>>
<<SetLookDirection NPC_Name.Isla LookDirection.Right>>
<<wait 1>>
Owen: Walter! Didn't have you pegged as a Tuesday night man.
<<SetLookDirection NPC_Name.Walter LookDirection.Left>>
Walter: Every night's a Tuesday when you're my age, son.
Isla: That's either very wise or very sad.
Walter: Both, probably.

// ── [SHOWCASE: Switch_Camera FarRightCam — focus Walter] ─
<<Switch_Camera CamController "FarRightCam">>
<<SetLookDirection NPC_Name.Walter LookDirection.Forward>>

Walter: And you — you're the new one. I'll have something {Order_Cocktail_OutDescription(NPC_Name.Walter)}.

-> Of course, coming right up.
    Player: Right away, sir.
    <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Walter "neutral">>
    Walter: "Sir." I could get used to that.
-> Any more details?
    Player: Anything more specific you're after?
    Walter: That IS specific. Get to work.
-> I'll see what I can do.
    Player: I'll do my best.
    <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Walter "neutral">>
    Walter: See that you do.

<<Reset_Camera CamController>>
<<Switch_Camera CamController "MainCam">>
<<Fix_Camera CamController false>>
<<wait_for_task SystemGame>>
<<Fix_Camera CamController true>>
<<Switch_Camera CamController "FarRightCam">>

// ── [SHOWCASE: Satisfaction If/Else — Walter + multi-NPC reactions] ──
<<if $satisfaction == Satisfaction.Perfect>>
    <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Walter "happy">>
    Walter: ...Well. That is exactly right.
    <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Owen "happy">>
    Owen: High praise from Walter. Rarer than the drink itself.
    <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Isla "happy">>
    Isla: We're witnessing history!
    <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Walter "neutral">>
    Walter: Don't push it.
    -> That means a lot coming from you.
        Player: That means a lot coming from you, sir.
        <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Walter "happy">>
        Walter: Don't let it go to your head. ...Good work.
    -> Just doing my job.
        Player: Just doing my job.
        Walter: And doing it well. Don't stop.
<<elseif $satisfaction == Satisfaction.Acceptable>>
    <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Walter "neutral">>
    Walter: Mm. Passable.
    <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Owen "neutral">>
    Owen: Coming from Walter, that's basically a five-star review.
    Walter: It is not.
    <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Isla "happy">>
    Isla: It kind of is though.
    Walter: ...Drink your cocktails, both of you.
    -> I'll keep improving.
        Player: I'll keep working on it.
        <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Walter "neutral">>
        Walter: See that you do. There's potential here.
    -> Appreciate the honesty.
        Player: Thanks for the honest feedback.
        Walter: Always. It's the only kind worth giving.
<<elseif $satisfaction == Satisfaction.Fail>>
    <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Walter "upset">>
    Walter: ...No. No, that's not right at all.
    <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Owen "neutral">>
    Owen: He sort of warned you.
    <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Isla "neutral">>
    Isla: To be fair, mine wasn't perfect either.
    Walter: Standards, people. Standards.
    -> Let me try again.
        Player: Let me make you another.
        <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Walter "neutral">>
        Walter: Please. And take your time this round.
    -> What specifically went wrong?
        Player: What should I fix?
        Walter: Everything. But start with the basics.
<<endif>>

<<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Walter "neutral">>
<<Reset_Variable SystemGame>>

// ── [SHOWCASE: SetLookDirection ทุกตัวพร้อมกัน + Wrap Up] 
<<Switch_Camera CamController "CenterCam">>

Walter: You know, I've been coming to bars like this for forty years.
<<SetLookDirection NPC_Name.Walter LookDirection.Left>>
<<wait 0.4>>
<<SetLookDirection NPC_Name.Owen LookDirection.Left>>
<<SetLookDirection NPC_Name.Isla LookDirection.Left>>
<<wait 0.8>>
Walter: Seen good bartenders, bad ones. Everything in between.
<<SetLookDirection NPC_Name.Walter LookDirection.Forward>>
<<SetLookDirection NPC_Name.Owen LookDirection.Forward>>
<<SetLookDirection NPC_Name.Isla LookDirection.Forward>>

Owen: And where do we rank so far?
Walter: ...Ask me again in a few months.

// ── [SHOWCASE: Option Timeout ในฉาก Wrap Up] ─────────────
-> Hope to see you all again soon. ?
    Player: Hope to see you all again soon.
    <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Walter "happy">>
    Walter: If the drinks keep improving — certainly.
    <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Owen "happy">>
    Owen: I'll be back tomorrow. This place grows on you.
    <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Isla "happy">>
    Isla: Same! This was really fun.
-> Really glad you all came in tonight. ?
    Player: Really glad you all came in tonight.
    <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Isla "happy">>
    Isla: Us too! Right, Walter?
    <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Walter "happy">>
    Walter: ...Sure. Right.
-> You know where to find me. ?
    Player: You know where to find me.
    <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Owen "happy">>
    Owen: Ha! Confidence. Good.
-> No rush — take your time. #fallback
    Player: No rush, stay as long as you like.
    <<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Walter "neutral">>
    Walter: Don't mind if I do.

// ── [SHOWCASE: MoveOut ทุกตัวละคร] ──────────────────────
<<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Owen "neutral">>
<<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Isla "neutral">>
<<SetEmotion NPC_Name.Walter "neutral">>

Owen: Right then. Night.
<<MoveOut NPC_Name.Owen>>

Isla: Byeee! See you next time!
<<MoveOut NPC_Name.Isla>>

Walter: Mm. Not bad.
<<MoveOut NPC_Name.Walter>>

<<Switch_Camera CamController "MainCam">>
<<Fix_Camera CamController false>>
<<wait 3>>
<<Can_End_Shift SystemGame>>

===
